<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Porus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died c. 317 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Porus was an Indian king who ruled the land between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jhelum">Jhelum</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chenab">Chenab</a> rivers in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a>. In 326 BCE he fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-hydaspes">Battle of the Hydaspes</a> with a large army including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-elephant">war elephants</a>, and was defeated. Impressed by his bearing, Alexander restored him to his kingdom and enlarged it. He was murdered by the Macedonian officer Eudemus around 317 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/porus.jpg" alt="Porus" width="320" height="323" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User PHGCOM · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Porus_alexander_coin.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
